description: 'The `take` keyword does not parse when used in function-call argument
  position: `consume(take v)` → "expected comma, got v". Fix: add `take EXPR` to the
  expression precedence ladder at the unary tier in `src/parser/expr.rs` (same level
  as `not`). Without this, the ownership story is unreachable from normal user code.
  Add conformance test: `consume(take v)` must compile and the value must be moved
  (not copyable after). (review/14_findings.md P0-5, review/15_roadmap.md A.5)'
